to testing, expect changes/rough edges; single CTA \u003ca class=\\\"instui-button\\\"-styled\u003e \\\"Sign up\\\" -\u003e https://forms.gle/jXYJN6NNQFnaYCPa8 (inline padding/bg/border/radius/font, mso-padding-alt, bulletproof table cell); secondary paragraph \\\"Not interested in actively participating but want to stay informed about updates? Follow along\\\" -\u003e https://community.instructure.com/en/group/70-canvas-mcp; sign-off \\\"Instructure Product Team\\\".\\n4. Dark: @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) + [data-ogsc] overrides for page/card/text/link/button using dark map.\\n\\nVerification: open in browser (light/dark via devtools emulation); check no var(, no external CSS, no \u003cscript\u003e; optional Litmus/Email on Acid.\\n\\nExcluded: generator script, repo changes, changeset, unsubscribe footer, plain-text version.\\n\"}","name":"memory","result":{"output":"","status":"success"},"type":"tool_use"}]}
{"v":1,"agent":"copilot-cli","cli_version":"0.11.2","type":"assistant","ts":"2026-09-25T18:18:39.803Z","id":"847288d5-3f47-4745-9a1b-03d2fe33eeeb","content":[{"text":"## Plan: Canvas MCP invite email with inlined pantoken styles\n\nA single static HTML email at `~/Desktop/canvas-mcp-invite.html`, outside the repo. Every style is inline and uses concrete light-mode values from `@pantoken/email`. Dark mode sits in a small `\u003cstyle\u003e` block as an enhancement, so clients that strip `\u003cstyle\u003e` still get the full light design.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Get the token values.** Run a one-off `node -e` that imports [platforms/email/dist/index.mjs](platforms/email/dist/index.mjs) and prints the `light` and `dark` values for these keys:\n   - **Page and card:** `colorBackgroundPage`, `colorBackgroundBase`, `colorStrokeMuted`, `borderRadiusLg`\n   - **Text and link:** `colorTextBase`, `colorTextMuted`, `colorTextInteractiveNavigationPrimaryBase`\n   - **Button:** `colorBackgroundInteractiveActionPrimaryBase`, `colorTextInteractiveActionPrimaryBase`, `colorStrokeInteractiveActionPrimaryBase`, `componentBaseButtonBorderRadius`, `componentBaseButtonMediumHeight`, `componentBaseButtonMediumPaddingHorizontal`, `componentBaseButtonMediumFontSize`, `fontWeightInteractive`\n   - **Type and spacing:** `fontFamilyBase`, `spacingSpaceSm` through `spacingSpaceXl`\n2. **Build the email frame** (*depends on 1*):\n   - A doctype plus `color-scheme` / `supported-color-schemes` meta tags.\n   - A hidden preheader: \"Get early access to test the experimental Canvas MCP server.\"\n   - A centered 600px layout built from `role=\"presentation\"` tables.\n   - A logo header `\u003cimg\u003e` with a placeholder PNG `src` for you to replace. It's sized 155×39, half the SVG's 310×79, with `alt=\"Canvas\"`.\n   - Atkinson Hyperlegible first in the font stack, with system fallbacks.\n3. **Write the body** (*depends on 2*):\n   - **Heading:** \"Help test the official Canvas MCP server.\"\n   - **Why you're getting this:** you said you're interested in the community.\n   - **Experimental callout:** a bordered, muted box saying it's experimental, you'll get early access to testing, and things will change.\n   - **Single CTA:** \"Sign up\" linking to https://forms.gle/jXYJN6NNQFnaYCPa8. It's an `\u003ca\u003e` inside a table cell with the button's inline styles and `mso-padding-alt` for Outlook, mirroring the base rules in [button.css](formats/components/src/components/button/button.css).\n   - **Below the CTA:** your \"Not interested in actively participating…\" line, with a \"Follow along\" link to https://community.instructure.com/en/group/70-canvas-mcp.\n   - **Sign-off:** \"Instructure Product Team.\"\n4. **Add dark mode** (*depends on 3*): a `\u003cstyle\u003e` block with `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` plus `[data-ogsc]` overrides that use the `dark` values (with `!important`) for the page, card, text, link, and button, targeted by class hooks.\n\n**Verification**\n1. Search the file for `var(`, `\u003clink`, and `\u003cscript`. None should appear.\n2. Open it in a browser and toggle light/dark with DevTools color-scheme emulation.\n3. Optionally, test Gmail, Outlook, and Apple Mail rendering in Litmus or Email on Acid.\n\n**Decisions**\n- It's a static HTML file, not a generator script, and it doesn't touch the repo, so no changeset or `@pantoken/ai` update.\n- The logo uses a PNG placeholder because pantoken ships logos only as SVG, which Gmail and Outlook won't render.\n- It's out of scope: an unsubscribe footer and a plain-text version.","type":"text"}]}
